Packages/
sourcemap.json
*.blend1
__pycache__/

# reference study media (recordings, frames): private, never in the repo
research/

# Obsidian (the repo is the vault): the settings are kept, each person's window layout and the trash are not
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.trash/
# the plugins are kept whole (code and settings), so a fresh clone opens with every plugin ready
# except Excalidraw's settings: it counts every drawing opened, so the file changes on both PCs and would clash
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-excalidraw-plugin/data.json
/.tmp_run_args.json

# regenerated on every render (the GIF in docs/attachments is the record)
art/creatures/*/renders/swim_*/
# Claude's scratch files
/.tmp_*
# renders and checks the creature scripts make while a model is being built (tools/art/voxel_paths.py)
/work/
art/map/hub_looks/
# the map chat's study variants: a 1-25 MB parts.json each, which its tools make again (2026-11-22: left out of the
# shared repo, as art/map/hub_looks is; their renders, sheets and specs are kept)
art/map/**/parts.json
!art/map/greybox/parts.json
# each PC's own Claude settings (the shared ones are .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json
